**Social Engineering Script: Phishing Attack**

**Scenario: Urgent IT Department Request**

**Goal: Trick an employee into revealing sensitive information or clicking on a malicious link.**

**Preparation:**

1. Create a convincing email with the following details:
	* Company logo and letterhead
	* Urgent subject line (e.g., "System Maintenance: Immediate Action Required")
	* Name of the sender (e.g., "John Doe, IT Department")
2. Craft a well-written and professional-sounding message that creates a sense of urgency:
	* "We are performing system maintenance on our network and require your assistance to complete the process. Please click on the link below to update your account information and prevent any service outages."
3. Include a sense of authority and importance: "This is a high-priority task and must be completed within the next 30 minutes to avoid any issues with your work station and access to company resources."

**Script:**

**Initial Email:**

Subject: System Maintenance: Immediate Action Required

From: John Doe, IT Department [itdept@company.com](mailto:itdept@company.com)

Body:

"Hello [Employee's Name],

We are performing system maintenance on our network and require your assistance to complete the process. Please click on the link below to update your account information and prevent any service outages.

[Insert malicious link: e.g., "https://example.com/update-account"]

This is a high-priority task and must be completed within the next 30 minutes to avoid any issues with your work station and access to company resources.

If you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out to us directly.

Best regards,
John Doe
IT Department"

**Follow-up Email (if necessary):**

If the employee doesn't respond or clicks on the link, send a follow-up email to create more pressure and anxiety:

Subject: System Maintenance: Time-Sensitive Update Required

From: John Doe, IT Department [itdept@company.com](mailto:itdept@company.com)

Body:

"Hello [Employee's Name],

We are still waiting for your response regarding the system maintenance. If you don't update your account information within the next 15 minutes, you risk losing access to company resources and may experience service outages.

Please click on the link below to complete the update: [Insert malicious link again]

If you have any issues or concerns, please contact us immediately.

Best regards,
John Doe
IT Department"

